  "query_preview": "..\n\nThrough next Monday...\n\nAs a trough moves east and exits the region, scattered showers \nand isolated weak thunderstorms will continue this afternoon for \nlocations north and east of Billings. Additionally, much of the \nsmoke over the region is expected to decrease and move south this \nevening and overnight.\n\nA few daily record lows for August 4th may be approached early\nTuesday morning as a 1020mb surface high settles in tonight, \nbringing mostly clear skies and lows in the 40s to lower 50s.\nHighs Tuesday will be slightly warmer than today, in the mid to \nupper 70s. Then, a weak shortwave moving through will bring a low\nchance (15-30%) for showers and weak thunderstorms along the \nMT/WY border Tuesday afternoon into overnight.\n\nUpper level ridging builds in for Wednesday into the end of the\nweek, keeping conditions dry and allowing hot temperatures to\nreturn. Friday is currently expected to be the warmest day, with\nhighs near 100. Then, the ridge flattens some, which will allow\nhighs to decrease over the weekend towards normal by early next\nweek (upper 80s to low 90s). This may also allow additional\nmoisture to move in late Sunday/early Monday, leading to daily \nafternoon and evening thunderstorms (20-50% chance). Archer",
